## Why This Is Asked

Rationale: session fixation is a common beginner pitfall when using server-side sessions. The plan demonstrates practical, verifiable steps and testing.

## Key Concepts

- Session fixation and rotation
- HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookie flags
- Server-side session store (Redis)
- Per-user session invalidation
- Basic automated tests for session validity

## Code Example

```javascript
// Express-like sketch
app.post('/login', async (req,res)=>{
  const user = await authenticate(req.body);
  if(!user) return res.status(401).end();
  const sessionId = generateSessionId();
  await redis.set(`sess:${user.id}`, sessionId, 'EX', 3600);
  res.cookie('session', sessionId, { httpOnly: true, secure: true, sameSite: 'Strict' });
  res.json({ ok: true });
});

app.use((req,res,next)=>{
  const sid = req.cookies?.session;
  if(!sid) return res.status(401).end();
  // validate sid against Redis
  // deny if not found or mismatched
  next();
});
```

